# The repo carries tools and English data only. Game data - disc images,
# extractions, patched output, Japanese script dumps, the Sega CD corpus,
# savestates, RAM dumps, memory cards - never enters it.

# Disc images and everything extracted from them (all four platforms)
discs/
patched/
release/

# Reference corpora that are not ours: community JP dumps, the Sega CD
# script, third-party walkthroughs (routing input for the headless pilot)
reference/
guides/

# Scratch: RAM/VRAM dumps, JP reference text (work/ref), per-batch
# translation scripts (they quote source lines), bookmarks (work/states),
# the memory-card library (work/saves), harness runs. Real source never
# lives here any more - it moved to lib/, ps1/, pce/.
#
# Except the build's own inputs that are neither game content nor
# regenerable exactly (2026-09-12, after the junction deletion took them):
# the pair-glyph table every translation was fitted against (a rebuild
# can shift pairs and budgets), the disc's file map, the voice census,
# jPSXdec's index of the original disc and the font's slot table.
work/*
!work/pair_table.json
!work/free_slots.json
!work/lba_map.json
!work/master_lines.json
!work/snatcher_jp.idx
!work/font_table.txt

# Stale bulk parked during the 2026-09-10 reorganisation (old CHDs and
# releases, emulator installs, one-off logs). Delete when sure.
archive/

# Emulators and their state. Third-party binaries are not ours to
# redistribute, and memory cards / savestates are game data.
mednafen/
duckstation/
NO$PSX.*
no$psx.*
MEMCARD/
memcards/
savestates/
*.mcd
*.sav
*.exe
*.dll

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.tmp

# Third-party tools that the build scripts download on demand:
# jPSXdec (ps1/tools/fmvtext.py), chdman (Convert-To-CHD.bat),
# xdelta3 (Make-Patch.bat)
lib/jpsxdec/
lib/chdman/
lib/xdelta/

# jPSXdec / emulator droppings (written to the CWD of the run)
.sentry-native/
debug00.log
index.log
replace.log
save.log

# Windows fonts a few pictures are rendered in (lib/sysfont.py): copies the
# builder supplies, never redistributed
fonts/

# machine-specific dev paths (lib/devpaths.py); local_paths.example.json shows the keys
local_paths.json
